  "context": "UI panel tests (PyQt/PySide). Important context:\n\n- Worker QThreads must be retained against GC or the test process exits 255; modal dialogs (exec()) block and hang the test (exit 124). Do NOT introduce real modal dialog .exec() calls or unretained QThreads. When a behavior is driven by a dialog/elevation/UAC prompt, the dialog/transport is the ONLY allowed double - stub it at that boundary and assert the real downstream effect.\n\n- Never mock the panel/widget class under test. Drive the real widget: construct it, call its real slots/methods, and assert the real resulting model/state/signal. Use qtbot if available, or call slots directly and assert the widget's real attributes/model contents.\n\n- Tests run headless in the sandbox (offscreen Qt platform). Tests that genuinely require a display server, a real GPU, or external GUI services may skip as environment-capability gaps - keep those skips. Everything else must run and assert concrete state, not just isinstance/not-None.\n\n- QEMU/external-emulator tests legitimately skip when QEMU is not installed in the sandbox - keep those skips."
